    "result_text": "Build succeeds, all tests green (the acceptance suite is the only test class, both tests pass).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `registrationDate` on owner creation: when omitted, it defaults to the server's current date; when supplied it's preserved. It round-trips as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (JSON serialization of `java.time.LocalDate`).\n\n**Behaviour change (kept in small, low-complexity units):**\n- `BuildOwner.java` \u2014 the one function I modified. `BuildOwner` has no other methods (WMC_other = 0), so the default-date `if` costs almost nothing structurally:\n  ```java\n  Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);\n  if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n      owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());\n  }\n  built.set(owner);\n  ```\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `registrationDate` field plus a plain getter/setter (each CC = 1). No existing method touched.\n\n**Wiring (no cyclomatic weight):**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to `OwnerFields`, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` accepts it and `OwnerDto` returns it. MapStruct maps it automatically by name \u2014 the mapper needed no change, and no new pipeline step/YAML was required.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column, keeping all four dialects in sync (as they already are for `email`).\n- `db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql` \u2014 the seed rows use positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so each got a trailing `NULL` for the new column (h2/postgres use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nI deliberately put the defaulting logic in the tiny `BuildOwner` class rather than a new pipeline step (avoids an extra file) or the large `Owner` entity (which would pay for the whole class's complexity), keeping the WMC_other lever near zero.\n\nOne thing to flag so it's your call, not a silent choice: I updated all four DB dialects for consistency rather than only the test-exercised `hsqldb`. That touches more files, but leaving the entity's column absent from postgres/mysql/h2 would break inserts on those backends \u2014 a real defect. If you'd rather minimize footprint to just the tested path, I can revert the h2/postgres/mysql schema (and mysql data) edits.",
